      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logan%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settlers sent by Brigham Young founded Logan in 1859, scouting a fort site along the Logan River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logan%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Utah State University, founded in 1888 as the Agricultural College of Utah, now sits on Logan’s main campus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logan%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Logan River carved through ancient glacial deposits, leaving steep slopes and a low‑lying bottomland that defines the city’s terrain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
